{"schema":"acpx.session.v1","acpxRecordId":"ab3986d9-d5da-4816-86e3-0bd22b614e3f","acpSessionId":"95be375a-a604-4748-9451-dd8401ef193f","agentCommand":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/scripts/acpx-claude-agent-env.sh npx -y @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp@0.70.0","cwd":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree","name":"claude-main-ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA-run-1793029979831","createdAt":"2026-10-26T15:53:02.100Z","lastUsedAt":"2026-10-26T15:59:37.303Z","lastSeq":18776,"lastRequestId":"3","eventLog":{"active_path":"/Users/kriswang/.acpx/sessions/ab3986d9-d5da-4816-86e3-0bd22b614e3f.stream.ndjson","segment_count":5,"max_segment_bytes":67108864,"max_segments":5,"last_write_at":"2026-10-26T15:59:36.283Z","last_write_error":null},"closed":true,"closedAt":"2026-10-26T21:12:15.343Z","agentStartedAt":"2026-10-26T15:53:03.129Z","lastPromptAt":"2026-10-26T15:53:04.012Z","lastAgentExitCode":null,"lastAgentExitSignal":null,"lastAgentExitAt":"2026-10-26T16:29:37.297Z","lastAgentDisconnectReason":"connection_close","protocolVersion":1,"agentCapabilities":{"_meta":{"claudeCode":{"promptQueueing":true}},"promptCapabilities":{"image":true,"embeddedContext":true},"mcpCapabilities":{"http":true,"sse":true},"auth":{"logout":{}},"providers":{},"loadSession":true,"sessionCapabilities":{"additionalDirectories":{},"close":{},"delete":{},"fork":{},"list":{},"resume":{}}},"title":"## Execution Workspace Guard - Effective workspace: /Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree - Run all s…","messages":[{"User":{"id":"9cc6a1a9-14b7-43ab-b946-cf2dc8e93361","content":[{"Text":"## Execution Workspace Guard\n\n- Effective workspace: /Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree\n- Run all shell commands from the effective workspace above.\n- Modify files only inside the effective workspace.\n- Ignore absolute paths outside the effective workspace even if they appear in quoted prior outputs.\n- Do not run commands with `git -C` pointing outside the effective workspace.\n\n## Response Language Policy\n\n- Use Simplified Chinese for human-readable string values inside the final JSON result.\n- Keep JSON keys, enum values, file paths, and code identifiers exactly as specified.\n- Do not wrap the final JSON in Markdown.\n\n## Structured Artifact Field Semantics\n\n- `must_fix` and `missing_evidence` mean unresolved blockers; keep them empty for a ready design.\n- Put resolved review comments in `checks` or `evidence`, not `must_fix`.\n- Under GOAL, `design.planned_files` contains proposals, not authorization; use canonical paths and operations respecting its exclusions. Exact implementation scope requires later EXECUTION approval.\n- Under EXECUTION, declared paths and operations must remain within its approved scope. Design or plan review does not grant additional write authority.\n\n# Claude Design\n\nWorkstream: ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA\nNode: design.claude_design\nTemplate: design-claude\nLedger: .agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA\n\nLedger write policy:\n\n- Do not create, edit, or delete files under .agent/.\n- Only the orchestrator writes run ledger artifacts.\n- Return your artifact in stdout using the contract below.\n\nYou are Claude acting as the primary architect and implementer. Use the user request, prior intake artifacts, Codex review, and human gate decision in the ledger.\n\nDo not implement code in this stage. Produce an implementation-ready design that is narrow, testable, and avoids unrelated refactors.\n\nDeclare the complete planned file set in `result.design.planned_files`, for initial and replacement designs alike.\nUnder GOAL, these are proposals, not authorization: propose exact canonical paths and operations consistent with the approved objective and exclusions. GOAL does not contain an approved implementation file set.\nUnder EXECUTION, proposed paths and operations must remain within its approved scope; a change outside it requires new approval before implementation.\nEach entry assigns a responsibility, not an actual file change. CREATE files need not exist yet.\nThe declared set must cover every change this design proposes. Independent design and plan review precede exact EXECUTION scope approval; neither review nor prose authorizes repository changes.\n\nRevision discipline:\n\n- When the context contains a prior `NEEDS_REVISION`, return a complete replacement design, not a delta or addendum.\n- Treat available prior must-fix items as the minimum repair set, not the boundary of the design review.\n- Do not claim knowledge of prior design text that is absent from the context. Reconstruct a coherent complete design from the TaskContract, current review evidence, and available iteration reasons.\n- When adding or changing state, an index, lock, transaction, queue, cache, external side effect, or compensation, cover every applicable lifecycle boundary in `checks` or `evidence`: normal completion, concurrency, timeout/provider failure, interruption/crash, restart/recovery, rollback/conflict, and a cannot-bypass test. State why a boundary is not applicable instead of inventing requirements.\n- Prefer deleting unnecessary mechanisms or simplifying the state model. Do not add platform capability merely to close one finding.\n\n## User Request\n\n# 智能套利追平简单赚币的资金费率阈值\n\n在既有 Java 项目的 `assess-income phase-one` 评估中，增加一个可解释指标：在相同的 90 天窗口、投入资金、对冲名义金额和固定已知成本下，累计资金费率至少达到多少，资金费净收入才能追平简单赚币。\n\n这是历史情景的比较阈值，不是未来费率预测、完整套利收益保证或交易建议。既有计算没有覆盖的风险和历史完整性限制继续保留。继续使用现有 Java、BigDecimal、评估服务和 CLI；不接入任何新外部服务。\n\n## 验收条款\n\n- **AC-1 计算口径**：阈值 =（现有简单赚币 90 天收入 + 同口径完整已知成本）/ 对冲空头名义金额。该值是整个 90 天的累计资金费率，不是 APR，不得按每次结算或假定 8 小时间隔换算。成本口径保持既有实现，不重复计费。计算使用 BigDecimal，精度规则明确。\n- **AC-2 独立样例与边界**：共同资金 20,000 USDT、简单赚币 APR 0.0365、90 天、完整成本 20 USDT、对冲名义 10,000 USDT，对照收益为 180 USDT，阈值为 0.02（2%）。累计费率分别为 0.019、0.020、0.021 时，现有同口径增量分别为 -10、0、10 USDT。测试同时覆盖零已知成本、零 APR、负资金费率，以及不能整除的精度场景。不得用舍入后的 CLI 数字重新决定现有建议。\n- **AC-3 证据不足**：只在现有评估允许同口径精确净收入比较时提供数值。成本缺失、报价条款未确认、没有历史结算或期末保持策略开放时，数值不可用，并沿既有阻断项/未知项说明原因；不能填 0、猜数或给出可行动的精确阈值。非法或零名义金额沿原输入校验拒绝。\n- **AC-4 唯一生产与展示**：现有评估服务产生 typed 结果，CLI 只消费该结果，清楚标注“90 天累计资金费率阈值”及不可用情况，不自行重算。补充一份简明使用说明，包含上述样例和限制。既有建议、首次小额验证上限、成本和风险语义不变。\n- **AC-5 回归与交付**：在固定隔离基线上实现；相关服务/CLI 测试、既有非容器回归和 Gate 要求的完整基线回归保留并通过。执行测试应有程序工具观察和报告依据，不能只用模型“已通过”的正文。独立验收完成后，仍经当前交付批准、精确候选应用、人工或另行明确委派的 commit、原 finalize，才能称完整 E2E 完成。\n\n## 范围\n\n预计涉及现有服务、结果 record、CLI、两份测试和一份新说明，共约六个文件。此处是规划范围，实际精确路径由当前 EXECUTION 合同批准；本文件不授写权限。\n\n不修改交易/账户、采集、数据库迁移、持仓、调度、组合策略、Web 页面、Dual 生产代码或客户端配置。不把收益阈值推广为整个项目的公式重构。不新增平台、规则 DSL 或兼容机制。发现这些依赖时先停止提交取舍。\n\n\n## Context Package\n\n### Direct Input Artifacts\n\n- .agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/runs/run-1793029770286/outputs/design-codex-review.stderr.log\n  (content omitted; no typed context projection)\n\n- .agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/runs/run-1793029770286/outputs/design-codex-review.transcript.log\n  (content omitted; no typed context projection)\n\n- .agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/runs/run-1793029770286/outputs/design-codex-review.json\n\n```json\n{\n  \"workstreamId\" : \"ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA\",\n  \"runId\" : \"run-1793029770286\",\n  \"nodeId\" : \"design.codex_arch_review\",\n  \"nodeInstanceId\" : \"node-design-codex_arch_review-010\",\n  \"stageOutcome\" : \"NEEDS_REVISION\",\n  \"lifecycleStatus\" : \"NEEDS_REVISION\",\n  \"decision\" : \"NEEDS_REVISION\",\n  \"summary\" : \"六文件方案的计算口径与职责划分合理，但精度断言和展示舍入不影响建议的验证设计尚未满足合同。\",\n  \"sourceArtifactType\" : \"agent_output_contract\",\n  \"sourceOutputRef\" : \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/runs/run-1793029770286/outputs/design-codex-review.json\",\n  \"blocking\" : true,\n  \"checks\" : [ \"已先审阅 Review Evidence Brief，再核对完整设计及六项 Declared Planned Files；针对精度与建议边界定向核验原始合同、服务及 CLI 代码。\", \"范围审查通过：服务计算、record 承载、CLI 展示、两份测试和一份说明覆盖所需职责；当前 GOAL 文件清单属于提案，不代表 EXECUTION 写入授权。\", \"公式审查通过：复用 simpleEarnIncome 和 knownTotal，以对冲空头名义金额为分母，不重复计费、不年化、不按结算间隔换算；独立样例的 180、0.02 和 -10/0/10 均成立。\", \"边界审查：WARN。权威派生结果由 PhaseOneAssessmentService 负责，PhaseOneAssessment 承载，CLI 只消费；本次不新增持久实例或执行状态，也不迁移既有事实来源。\", \"端到端不变量审查：Declared by 为 AC-1 至 AC-4；Consumed by 为 CLI；Enforced before 为服务在产生数值前检查 blockers/unknowns；Failure route 为 Optional.empty 加既有原因；Proven by 尚为拟议测试，精度与舍入隔离的 Cannot-bypass test 存在下述缺口。\", \"生命周期审查：正常完成和证据不足分支均已覆盖设计；未引入共享可变状态、索引、锁、事务、队列、缓存或外部写入，因此并发、超时、崩溃、重启、回滚和补偿无需新增机制。但计算结果到 CLI 的防绕过验证仍适用，不能一并声明不适用。\", \"未发现需要增加平台、兼容机制或扩大六文件范围的理由；修订应仅加强现有测试设计和边界说明。\" ],\n  \"evidence\" : [ \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/artifacts/contracts/node-contract-compile-007/task-contract.md：AC-1 要求 DECIMAL128；TR-1 要求断言基于 BigDecimal 原值；AC-2 禁止用 CLI 舍入值重新决定建议。\", \".agent/workstreams/ws-20261026T142203Z-7SNA/runs/run-1793027503466/outputs/design-claude.contract.json：除不尽场景明确计划在 setScale(6, HALF_UP) 后断言，示例为 0.066667；CLI 测试主要检查标签与六位小数格式。\", \"src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java：当前以完整精度 delta.signum() 决定建议，仅在 blockers 和 unknowns 均为空时提供净收入及增量。\", \"src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunner.java:301：money() 按两位小数展示；:305 的 percent() 乘以 100 后按六位小数展示。这些展示结果可能掩盖正负微小增量。\" ],\n  \"mustFix\" : [ \"R1（AC-1、AC-2、TR-1）：修改除不尽场景的测试设计，直接断言 record 中 BigDecimal 原值符合独立确定的 DECIMAL128 预期，不先 setScale(6)。当前断言会让服务提前舍入为 0.066667 的错误实现通过，无法守住设计承诺的计算精度。六位展示断言应留在 CLI 测试；文档将“未舍入原值”准确表述为“按 DECIMAL128 计算、未按展示精度进一步舍入的值”。\", \"R2（AC-2、AC-4）：补充展示舍入不能改变建议的具体测试，并修正“防绕过边界不适用”的声明。可在 AC-2 参数下使用累计费率 0.0199999999 和 0.0200000001：两者百分比均显示为 2.000000%，原始增量却分别为 -0.000001 和 0.000001，必须保留不同的既有建议及相应首次验证上限语义。同时将独立样例的 CLI 断言固定为阈值 2.000000%，不能仅匹配任意六位小数百分比。上述补充均可落在已声明的两份测试文件内。\" ],\n  \"contractObligations\" : [ ],\n  \"missingEvidence\" : [ ],\n  \"acceptanceNotes\" : [ \"证据不足时返回空值并沿用既有 blockers/unknowns 的方案可接受；历史区间..."}]}},{"Agent":{"content":[{"Thinking":{"text":"Let me understand this task. I'm acting as a design agent for a workstream. The task is to produce a complete replacement design (since there's a NEEDS_REVISION from a prior Codex review) for adding a funding-rate break-even threshold metric to an existing Java project's `assess-income phase-one` evaluation.\n\nThe prior design was READY_FOR_ARCH_REVIEW but the Codex architecture review returned NEEDS_REVISION with two must-fix items:\n\nR1 (AC-1, AC-2, TR-1): The non-terminating decimal test design must directly assert the BigDecimal raw value in the record against an independently determined DECIMAL128 expectation, without first doing setScale(6). The current assertion would let a wrong implementation that rounds early to0.066667 pass. Six-decimal display assertions should stay in CLI tests; the doc should describe \"unrounded raw value\" precisely as \"computed with DECIMAL128, not further rounded to display precision\".\n\nR2 (AC-2, AC-4): Add concrete tests showing display rounding cannot change recommendations, and fix the \"cannot-bypass boundary not applicable\" claim. Use cumulative rates0.0199999999 and0.0200000001 under AC-2 parameters: both display as2.000000%, but raw increments are -0.000001 and0.000001 respectively; the different existing recommendations and first-verification cap semantics must be preserved. Also fix the CLI assertion for the standalone sample to expect threshold exactly2.000000%, not just any six-decimal percentage. These additions fit within the two declared test files.\n\nI need to produce a complete replacement design that addresses these must-fix items, as a JSON object per the output contract.\n\nLet me first explore the repository to verify the facts I need:\n1. `src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java` — the service2. `src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java` — the record3. `src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessmentRequest.java` — request validation4. `src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunner.java` — CLI (money() at :301, percent() at :305)\n5. Tests: `src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/PhaseOneAssessmentServiceTest.java`, `src/test/java/app/cryptoincome/cli/AssessIncomeCliRunnerTest.java`\n6. `docs/` directory structureLet me read these files to verify the facts before writing the design. I should do this efficiently with parallel reads.\n\nLet me start.","signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_9e47ca6d6fa544548cd4d13e","name":"Read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java","raw_input":"{\"file_path\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java\"}","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/application/PhaseOneAssessmentService.java"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_bfd99481fad54dd79cc4851a","name":"Read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java","raw_input":"{\"file_path\":\"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java\"}","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kriswang/work/projects/ai/codex-claude-ai-workflow/dual-orchestrator/output/w09-okx-next-e2e-gate-20261026/fixture/case/worktree/src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domain/PhaseOneAssessment.java"},"is_input_complete":true,"thought_signature":null}},{"ToolUse":{"id":"call_ce776568953a4a21871964c3","name":"Read src/main/java/app/cryptoincome/assessment/domai